<section class="section section--warm">
  <div class="wrap--narrow stack-lg">
    <h2>When you should <em>not</em> sell to us</h2>
    <p>This is the part most cash-buyer websites leave out. Do not sell to us if:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your house is in good condition and you have two or three months.</strong>
      List it. Even after a 6% commission you will very likely net more than our offer.</li>
      <li><strong>You are only a little behind and can catch up.</strong> Call your servicer
      about a repayment plan or a loan modification first. Selling should be the fallback,
      not the first move.</li>
      <li><strong>You owe more than the house is worth.</strong> A cash sale usually cannot
      work. Ask your lender about a short sale.</li>
      <li><strong>One spouse can refinance and keep the house in a divorce.</strong> That is
      generally a better outcome than selling.</li>
      <li><strong>Your relocation package includes a guaranteed buyout.</strong> Compare it
      carefully. Sometimes it beats us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We will say all of this on the phone too. Telling someone the truth costs us one deal;
      taking a deal we shouldn't have costs us a reputation in a county this size.
    </p>

    <h3>A house we told the owner not to sell us</h3>
    <p>
      An older home out in the country on about six acres. Immaculate, a few spots
      wanted paint and the inside could have used updating eventually, but that was it. The
      basement had been redone and looked flawless. No deed restrictions, so you could put a
      horse on it. There was one odd add-on sitting a couple of inches higher than the rest
      of the house, which made no sense to us and made no difference to anybody.
    </p>
    <p>
      A cash offer on that house would have been pointless. Drone shots, a proper photo tour
      inside and out, and it was going to sell fast on the open market at a price no cash
      buyer would touch. So that is what we told the owner, and that is what happened. It
      sold quickly, the price was good, and he was happy.
    </p>
    {% if site.twoNumberPromise.enabled %}
    <p>
      We listed that one ourselves, which is the whole idea behind
      <a href="/two-number-promise/">the Two-Number Promise</a>. If the honest answer is
      "list it," we would rather be the ones who do than lose you to somebody else.
    </p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
