<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap--narrow stack-lg">
    <h2>When a cash sale genuinely is the better deal</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The house needs more work than you can fund, and retail buyers can't get financing on it.</li>
      <li>You have a hard deadline. A foreclosure sale date, a job start, a court date.</li>
      <li>The house is inherited, full, and three hours away.</li>
      <li>You have tenants you'd have to evict before you could list.</li>
      <li>You've already had a listing fall through at financing and can't take that risk again.</li>
      <li>You simply want it done, and the certainty is worth more to you than the last few percent.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

